From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:25:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gnss: add a type for the MT6797 DSP host protocol

The MT6797 GNSS DSP speaks a binary protocol with its host: the host loads
the DSP image and feeds it each second, and receives measurements, not
positions. It is not the MTK type, which a serial NMEA module uses, so
report it as its own type.
---
 Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-gnss | 1 +
 drivers/gnss/core.c                        | 1 +
 include/linux/gnss.h                       | 1 +
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-gnss b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-gnss
index 9650f3a7f..92e5fc268 100644
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-gnss
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-gnss
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ Description:
 			"NMEA"		NMEA 0183
 			"SiRF"		SiRF Binary
 			"UBX"		UBX
+			"MT6797"	MediaTek MT6797 DSP host protocol
 			======		===========
 
 		Note that also non-"NMEA" type receivers typically support a
diff --git a/drivers/gnss/core.c b/drivers/gnss/core.c
index 006f5533e..ec7e1fed2 100644
--- a/drivers/gnss/core.c
+++ b/drivers/gnss/core.c
@@ -334,6 +334,7 @@ static const char * const gnss_type_names[GNSS_TYPE_COUNT] = {
 	[GNSS_TYPE_SIRF]	= "SiRF",
 	[GNSS_TYPE_UBX]		= "UBX",
 	[GNSS_TYPE_MTK]		= "MTK",
+	[GNSS_TYPE_MT6797]	= "MT6797",
 };
 
 static const char *gnss_type_name(const struct gnss_device *gdev)
diff --git a/include/linux/gnss.h b/include/linux/gnss.h
index 36968a0f3..9b2b55d3a 100644
--- a/include/linux/gnss.h
+++ b/include/linux/gnss.h
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ enum gnss_type {
 	GNSS_TYPE_SIRF,
 	GNSS_TYPE_UBX,
 	GNSS_TYPE_MTK,
+	GNSS_TYPE_MT6797,
 
 	GNSS_TYPE_COUNT
 };
-- 
